      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FINAL DEADLINE NZ (7) landed a couple of Group races over the winter carnival and made a winning return to this track at his latest appearance, scoring by 2.4m. Has had seven weeks off but was kept ticking over with two trials and drops to a distance where he is unbeaten in four attempts. ATTACHMENT (3) led from the inside barrier and defied all challengers to score at this circuit and distance last start, arriving a neck ahead of his rivals. Has only once been beaten in his last six outings here and should go forward again from this draw. Big chance again. CAPTAIN SHUFFLES (8) won when second-up two back and got close to ATTACHMENT from this barrier last start. Danger. DASHING (11) cops a tough draw and was a beaten favourite last time but was racing well prior so don't give up on him yet.",
